1
00:00:00,933 --> 00:00:01,533
<i>Why do you have
to keep your worries</i>

2
00:00:01,667 --> 00:00:03,600
<i> about Jin Ho to yourself?</i>

3
00:00:03,733 --> 00:00:05,800
<i> You can tell Joey.</i>

4
00:00:05,933 --> 00:00:07,033
<i>No, I don't want to bother her.</i>

5
00:00:07,167 --> 00:00:07,967
<i> It's her family time.</i>

6
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,100
<i>I noticed you and Andrew
are close.</i>

7
00:00:10,233 --> 00:00:11,500
<i> Now that I know him,</i>

8
00:00:11,633 --> 00:00:12,700
<i> he's actually kind.</i>

9
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:14,000
<i> You're blushing, Joey.</i>

10
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:15,567
<i>This is the coordination letter.</i>

11
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,600
<i>I've also referred you
to the Drug Enforcement Unit</i>

12
00:00:17,733 --> 00:00:19,767
<i>in the North, located
in the town of Balmora.</i>

13
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:21,033
<i> Are you spying on me?</i>

14
00:00:21,167 --> 00:00:22,500
<i> Whatever you heard,</i>

15
00:00:22,633 --> 00:00:23,800
<i> it can't get out.</i>

16
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:26,133
<i>What's going on
in the town of Balmora?</i>

17
00:00:26,267 --> 00:00:28,133
<i>Don't worry, if I find out,
I'll tell you.</i>

18
00:00:28,267 --> 00:00:29,200
<i> I have to go now.</i>

19
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:30,433
<i> Just leave tomorrow.</i>

20
00:00:30,567 --> 00:00:32,033
<i>Dad, I'm going to give you
something.</i>

21
00:00:32,167 --> 00:00:33,500
<i>This is cute.
I'll go ahead.</i>

22
00:00:33,633 --> 00:00:34,833
<i>- Be careful, okay?
- Okay.</i>

23
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,267
<i> Don't worry, Berdugo.</i>

24
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,000
<i>We've prepared everything
for him.</i>

25
00:00:39,133 --> 00:00:41,767
<i> Make sure this won't fail.</i>

26
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:43,200
<i> You can count on it, Berdugo.</i>

27
00:00:43,333 --> 00:00:45,700
<i>Just think it's his first day on
the job,</i>

28
00:00:45,833 --> 00:00:47,500
<i> and his last day on earth.</i>

29
00:00:47,633 --> 00:00:49,167
<i>- Berdugo.
- Don't let it drag on.</i>

30
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,700
<i>- Finish him off.
- Sure, Boss.</i>

31
00:00:50,833 --> 00:00:53,267
<i> Don't involve my family!</i>

32
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:54,533
<i>Do you want to save your family?</i>

33
00:00:54,667 --> 00:00:56,133
<i> You're going to die!</i>

34
00:00:57,033 --> 00:00:58,167
<i> Chief sent me here</i>

35
00:00:58,300 --> 00:00:59,533
<i> to give you this.</i>

36
00:00:59,667 --> 00:01:00,733
<i> This is Miguel's badge.</i>

37
00:01:00,867 --> 00:01:01,800
<i> Why is it burned?</i>

38
00:01:01,933 --> 00:01:03,000
<i> They say a car exploded</i>

39
00:01:03,133 --> 00:01:04,167
<i> on the Bolagos highway.</i>

40
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:05,267
<i>They say the victim
is a police officer.</i>

41
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:06,467
<i> Where is Miguel?</i>

42
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:08,533
<i>It looks like Miguel was
involved in the explosion.</i>

43
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:10,267
<i> That can't be true!</i>

44
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,000
<i> My husband just left!</i>

45
00:01:12,133 --> 00:01:14,533
<i> Take us to Dad, please!</i>

46
00:01:36,433 --> 00:01:39,100
Is this all the evidence
you got, huh?

47
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:40,000
Nothing else?

48
00:01:40,133 --> 00:01:41,567
Nothing, Sir.

49
00:01:46,233 --> 00:01:47,700
Ma'am, this way.

50
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,200
Move aside.
Move.

51
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:53,933
Here, Ma'am.

52
00:01:56,467 --> 00:01:58,067
Joey...

53
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,567
Sir...

54
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:07,000
Dad...

55
00:02:08,433 --> 00:02:10,033
Is that Dad?

56
00:02:10,167 --> 00:02:12,300
Can I see him first?

57
00:02:12,433 --> 00:02:15,667
Joey, it's not a good idea
to see your father like this.

58
00:02:16,933 --> 00:02:18,567
You can't approach him.

59
00:02:19,633 --> 00:02:21,567
The plate number
has been confirmed,

60
00:02:22,067 --> 00:02:24,133
as well as the personal effects
that were taken.

61
00:02:24,267 --> 00:02:26,267
Everything belongs to Miguel.

62
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:29,500
I'm sorry, Clarissa, Joey.

63
00:02:35,933 --> 00:02:39,367
Can't I really see him first?

64
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:40,600
Not yet.

65
00:03:00,267 --> 00:03:02,300
Go ahead, sit down first.

66
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:24,267
<i>Dad, I'm going to give you
something...</i>

67
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:27,533
<i>so you won't forget mom and me.</i>

68
00:03:27,667 --> 00:03:29,733
<i> I really won't forget you,</i>

69
00:03:29,867 --> 00:03:32,867
<i> but this is cute.</i>

70
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,767
Mom, this is what I gave Dad.

71
00:04:01,233 --> 00:04:02,300
Boss Idol.

72
00:04:02,433 --> 00:04:04,033
I know Major Miguel Delgado.

73
00:04:04,167 --> 00:04:06,200
Let him in.
This way.

74
00:04:07,367 --> 00:04:08,800
Joey...

75
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:11,367
Joey...

76
00:04:14,967 --> 00:04:16,133
Andrew...

77
00:04:18,167 --> 00:04:20,000
It's dad...

78
00:04:23,133 --> 00:04:25,267
Chief, where are you taking
the remains?

79
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:27,333
To the crime lab for autopsy.

80
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:29,333
Standard procedure.

81
00:04:29,467 --> 00:04:31,600
Can't we see him...

82
00:04:31,733 --> 00:04:33,467
before you do that?

83
00:04:34,767 --> 00:04:38,300
Joey, Miguel's remains
are severely burned.

84
00:04:39,133 --> 00:04:41,433
It's better if you don't see him

85
00:04:41,567 --> 00:04:43,000
in that condition.

86
00:04:43,133 --> 00:04:45,000
And based on
the initial findings,

87
00:04:45,133 --> 00:04:47,267
there is a possibility
of foul play,

88
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:48,833
so we don't want to contaminate

89
00:04:48,967 --> 00:04:51,900
the evidence before the autopsy.

90
00:04:52,033 --> 00:04:54,033
After the process,

91
00:04:54,167 --> 00:04:56,367
we will release
the remains to you.

92
00:04:57,567 --> 00:05:02,100
So it would be better for you to
go home and rest.

93
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:03,933
Just a second...

94
00:05:04,067 --> 00:05:06,000
How did you know
it was really dad...

95
00:05:06,133 --> 00:05:08,467
if the body was so badly burned?

96
00:05:09,233 --> 00:05:13,467
Through the plate number
and personal effects.

97
00:05:14,267 --> 00:05:18,467
But we will still conduct
a DNA test for verification.

98
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:21,567
Chief, what do you mean
by foul play?

99
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:24,167
At first glance,
it looks like an accident.

100
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:26,133
There are skid marks
on the road.

101
00:05:26,267 --> 00:05:28,200
It looks like he lost control

102
00:05:28,333 --> 00:05:30,233
before he hit the wall.

103
00:05:30,367 --> 00:05:34,000
But we found a shell casing
at the crash site,

104
00:05:35,333 --> 00:05:38,533
And it's not from Miguel's
service firearm.

105
00:05:38,667 --> 00:05:41,067
That means there is a shooter.

106
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,400
It's a targeted attack.

107
00:05:43,533 --> 00:05:47,267
And it looks like he made sure
Miguel won't survive.

108
00:05:47,867 --> 00:05:51,333
I told him not to return
to the service!

109
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,900
If he hadn't left,
this wouldn't have happened!

110
00:06:06,633 --> 00:06:07,600
What's the news?

111
00:06:07,767 --> 00:06:08,967
Boss...

112
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:10,833
<i> his family is here...</i>

113
00:06:10,967 --> 00:06:12,233
<i> crying.</i>

114
00:06:12,367 --> 00:06:15,033
Are you sure Delgado is dead?

115
00:06:15,167 --> 00:06:16,367
I was only a few meters away

116
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:17,833
when his car exploded.

117
00:06:17,967 --> 00:06:19,033
Delgado was inside,

118
00:06:19,167 --> 00:06:21,700
so I'm sure he's dead.

119
00:06:21,833 --> 00:06:22,867
Good.

120
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,700
I'll increase your pay
for a job well done.

121
00:06:25,833 --> 00:06:27,767
Thank you, Berdugo.

122
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:56,000
Poor Delgado.

123
00:06:56,133 --> 00:06:57,967
He ended up
looking like a "sisig."

124
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:02,400
He's fond of explosions,
after all.

125
00:07:02,867 --> 00:07:04,800
He got what he deserved.

126
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,267
Cruz, bring them home.

127
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:17,233
- Ma'am, let's go.
- No, Cruz, I'll do it.

128
00:07:17,367 --> 00:07:19,000
I'll handle it.

129
00:07:19,133 --> 00:07:20,533
Let's go.

130
00:07:21,067 --> 00:07:22,767
Joey, I'm sorry for
what happened.

131
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:27,467
But I promise we'll help
with the investigation

132
00:07:28,033 --> 00:07:29,867
as much as we need to.

133
00:07:31,733 --> 00:07:33,367
Thanks, but...

134
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:36,867
there's no need to...

135
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:40,267
because the body is subject for
a DNA test, right?

136
00:07:40,733 --> 00:07:43,467
It's not yet certain
that it's really Dad.

137
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:45,633
Who knows, he survived, right?

138
00:07:45,767 --> 00:07:47,567
Dad might still be alive.

139
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:49,667
From the look of the car,

140
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:52,833
whoever was inside
would have been badly burned.

141
00:07:52,967 --> 00:07:54,167
It's definitely unrecognizable.

142
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:55,267
But based on the personal
effects,

143
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:57,400
there's no other possible victim

144
00:07:57,533 --> 00:07:58,500
but Major Miguel Delgado.

145
00:07:58,633 --> 00:07:59,900
I mean, who else, right?

146
00:08:00,033 --> 00:08:02,100
Elai, enough.

147
00:08:03,133 --> 00:08:04,367
Joey, sorry. I didn't mean it.

148
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:06,033
I was just basing it...

149
00:08:06,167 --> 00:08:07,333
- on facts.
- That's enough.

150
00:08:07,467 --> 00:08:09,133
Stop, stop, stop.

151
00:08:09,267 --> 00:08:10,567
It's okay.

152
00:08:11,733 --> 00:08:14,233
But it's probably
not that bad...

153
00:08:14,367 --> 00:08:16,833
to hope Dad is still alive,
right?

154
00:08:17,933 --> 00:08:19,633
Because he said...

155
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:21,733
this is...

156
00:08:22,267 --> 00:08:23,533
his last mission,

157
00:08:23,667 --> 00:08:25,100
and then...

158
00:08:26,733 --> 00:08:29,333
he's going to retire.

159
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,167
And...

160
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:33,700
he said we'll be together
with mom.

161
00:08:39,833 --> 00:08:42,800
And I believe dad
could still be alive.

162
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:46,267
Because they'll still have
his body be DNA tested?

163
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:48,500
So while, while there's
no proof yet,

164
00:08:48,633 --> 00:08:50,767
I believe dad is still alive.

165
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:52,633
He might not be dead yet.

166
00:08:53,633 --> 00:08:55,033
Right, Mom?

167
00:09:00,667 --> 00:09:02,067
Joey...

168
00:09:10,267 --> 00:09:12,033
Dad...

169
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:25,267
Dad...

170
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:41,767
Just one stand-upper,
then go home.

171
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:43,633
Then I'll go with you to edit.

172
00:09:43,933 --> 00:09:45,433
Copy, copy.

173
00:09:45,567 --> 00:09:46,867
Okay, I'll take care of it.

174
00:09:47,333 --> 00:09:48,633
Thanks.

175
00:09:50,533 --> 00:09:52,000
Andrew...

176
00:09:54,533 --> 00:09:56,267
Is Joey mad at me?

177
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:00,933
She's grieving.

178
00:10:01,633 --> 00:10:02,933
It's good that you're here.

179
00:10:07,133 --> 00:10:10,833
Well, you didn't just come here
for news.

180
00:10:11,333 --> 00:10:13,967
It's obvious that you
really care for Joey.

181
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,000
I was surprised.

182
00:10:16,133 --> 00:10:18,800
You're not usually like this
with our subjects.

183
00:10:18,933 --> 00:10:21,633
She's not just a subject.

184
00:10:22,967 --> 00:10:25,000
We've been through
a lot together.

185
00:10:25,133 --> 00:10:27,133
I've also met her family.

186
00:10:27,267 --> 00:10:29,433
So yes, we've become
really close.

187
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,000
If you're asking me
if I'm affected,

188
00:10:32,133 --> 00:10:33,767
I'm affected.

189
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,467
Yes, it shows.

190
00:10:37,767 --> 00:10:38,733
You really want to know

191
00:10:38,867 --> 00:10:41,233
what happened to Major Delgado.

192
00:10:41,367 --> 00:10:42,600
Come on, let's finish this.

193
00:10:42,733 --> 00:10:44,067
Let's go.

194
00:10:46,667 --> 00:10:48,400
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

195
00:10:48,933 --> 00:10:49,767
Okay.

196
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,000
Game?

197
00:10:51,133 --> 00:10:52,067
Ready?

198
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,467
Camera.

199
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,933
Rolling.

200
00:10:55,533 --> 00:10:57,767
Five, four, three...

201
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,700
A Bolagos Police officer

202
00:11:00,833 --> 00:11:03,433
is suspected of being killed
in an explosion incident

203
00:11:03,567 --> 00:11:06,633
along the Service Road tonight.

204
00:11:06,767 --> 00:11:08,267
According to authorities,

205
00:11:08,433 --> 00:11:10,800
it is believed
that Major Miguel Delgado

206
00:11:10,933 --> 00:11:12,800
of the Bolagos Police is the
victim

207
00:11:12,933 --> 00:11:15,000
after identifying
the burned out vehicle

208
00:11:15,133 --> 00:11:16,267
and some personal belongings

209
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:19,433
recovered from the scene
of the incident.

210
00:11:19,567 --> 00:11:21,533
<i>In an interview with Police
Chief Lansang of Bolagos,</i>

211
00:11:21,667 --> 00:11:24,467
<i>at first glance,
it seemed like an accident,</i>

212
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,200
<i>but there is evidence
that suggests</i>

213
00:11:26,333 --> 00:11:28,433
<i> foul play was possible.</i>

214
00:11:28,567 --> 00:11:31,500
<i>The victim's remains have been
brought to the crime laboratory</i>

215
00:11:31,633 --> 00:11:33,833
<i> for DNA confirmation.</i>

216
00:11:35,133 --> 00:11:36,367
My god...

217
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:37,667
Hon...

218
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,200
have you seen this?

219
00:11:39,333 --> 00:11:41,200
What is it?
Bad news?

220
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:42,567
Miguel, Clarissa's husband,

221
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:44,233
died last night.

222
00:11:44,367 --> 00:11:46,267
His vehicle exploded!

223
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,467
<i>Is this tragedy still connected</i>

224
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:50,233
<i> to the alleged syndicate?</i>

225
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:54,300
<i>That's what we're going
to find out, Ka-Tiradas.</i>

226
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:09,000
Hey! Peter, you're driving me
crazy!

227
00:12:09,133 --> 00:12:10,667
I've been looking for you
for some time now.

228
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:11,833
Where did you come from?

229
00:12:11,967 --> 00:12:13,967
You didn't even answer
my calls and texts.

230
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:15,433
You know, you're so noisy.

231
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,467
You know, I'm already annoyed

232
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:17,433
with Jin Ho's landlady,

233
00:12:17,567 --> 00:12:18,700
You're going to add to that.

234
00:12:18,833 --> 00:12:20,400
You're so noisy.

235
00:12:20,533 --> 00:12:22,867
Jin Ho's landlady?

236
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,100
Yes.

237
00:12:24,233 --> 00:12:26,400
I went to his old house to ask.

238
00:12:26,533 --> 00:12:27,833
Do you know what happened?

239
00:12:27,967 --> 00:12:29,733
I even ended up ebing the one
they took their anger out on.

240
00:12:29,867 --> 00:12:31,867
She said there was so much trash
Jin Ho left behind

241
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,267
that it was hard to clean up.

242
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,233
What? Is it my fault?

243
00:12:36,833 --> 00:12:37,867
You know, Andrew's right.

244
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,333
We don't really know
that Korean.

245
00:12:40,467 --> 00:12:42,900
Think about it, he passed by,
wreaked havoc,

246
00:12:43,033 --> 00:12:44,267
and then he suddenly left.

247
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:46,267
Oh, you're so great.

248
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:48,767
You're so deep.
What? Wreaked havoc?

249
00:12:48,933 --> 00:12:49,833
What's that? Typhoon?

250
00:12:49,967 --> 00:12:51,000
Then who are you?

251
00:12:51,133 --> 00:12:52,600
Sierra Madre?

252
00:12:52,733 --> 00:12:54,667
But admit it, just admit it.

253
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:55,967
You made an effort.

254
00:12:56,100 --> 00:12:57,133
Right, wrong?

255
00:12:57,267 --> 00:12:59,667
Of course, I'm worried, right?

256
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:02,033
I thought we were friends.

257
00:13:02,467 --> 00:13:04,933
but it turns out I was the only
one who thought of that.

258
00:13:07,067 --> 00:13:09,567
Wait, what do you need?
Why are you looking for me?

259
00:13:09,700 --> 00:13:10,867
What's that?

260
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:17,367
Look, this is the car
of Joey's dad.

261
00:13:25,633 --> 00:13:26,567
It's like...

262
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:29,133
it's like someone
really killed him.

263
00:13:40,867 --> 00:13:43,200
Mom, you should rest first.

264
00:13:46,867 --> 00:13:48,467
You too, Joey, okay?

265
00:14:47,133 --> 00:14:48,333
Peter?

266
00:14:48,967 --> 00:14:50,200
Joey...

267
00:14:50,667 --> 00:14:51,400
Joey, I heard about
what happened.

268
00:14:51,533 --> 00:14:52,533
How are you?

269
00:14:52,667 --> 00:14:53,867
How is Auntie?

270
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,867
I'll just ask permission from my
uncle, and then I'll go there.

271
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,700
No, that's not necessary.

272
00:14:58,400 --> 00:14:59,533
Why?

273
00:14:59,667 --> 00:15:01,900
Well, Father's body hasn't been
released yet,

274
00:15:02,367 --> 00:15:03,667
they say they still need
an autopsy

275
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:06,867
to make sure he was the victim.

276
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:09,067
I hope he's not,

277
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:11,233
because I feel sorry for
Uncle if that were the case.

278
00:15:11,367 --> 00:15:14,000
All his battles were
for the good.

279
00:15:14,133 --> 00:15:16,367
<i>His story shouldn't have
ended like this.</i>

280
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:18,600
That's why I don't believe it.

281
00:15:18,733 --> 00:15:19,967
What do you mean, Joey?

282
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:21,833
I don't know, Peter,

283
00:15:21,967 --> 00:15:23,200
but I have a really strong
feeling

284
00:15:23,333 --> 00:15:24,767
that Dad is still alive.

285
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:27,100
<i> So until I see his body,</i>

286
00:15:27,233 --> 00:15:29,367
<i> I won't believe it's him.</i>

287
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,200
<i> I will never lose hope</i>

288
00:15:31,333 --> 00:15:33,000
that my father is still alive.

289
00:16:02,633 --> 00:16:04,333
Mother, I'll take care of that.

290
00:16:04,467 --> 00:16:06,367
No, no, I'll take care of it.

291
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:08,900
I'm just removing the dirt
from the glass.

292
00:16:09,833 --> 00:16:11,433
Because it won't come off.

293
00:16:13,767 --> 00:16:16,267
Why won't it come off?
This isn't working.

294
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:17,233
We don't know...

295
00:16:17,367 --> 00:16:18,767
how to arrange the wake
of your father.

296
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:19,967
We don't know...

297
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:23,233
what he'll look like when
he comes back to us anymore.

298
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:28,067
Mother, do you really believe
that Dad is really dead?

299
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:32,333
Don't you want to hope
that he's still alive?

300
00:16:36,867 --> 00:16:38,467
I want to, Joey.

301
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:43,300
I really want to hope
that he's alive.

302
00:16:46,533 --> 00:16:51,400
But how after what we saw?

303
00:16:52,700 --> 00:16:56,233
His life has been in danger
several times,

304
00:16:56,933 --> 00:16:58,233
but he always makes it home.

305
00:16:58,367 --> 00:16:59,900
But now...

306
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:04,533
But Joey, it seems impossible.

307
00:17:25,900 --> 00:17:29,100
Still no update
on Major Delgado's autopsy.

308
00:17:30,033 --> 00:17:31,100
That's the thing.

309
00:17:32,233 --> 00:17:34,133
Twelve hours have passed.

310
00:17:35,267 --> 00:17:36,900
I thought they would
expedite it,

311
00:17:37,033 --> 00:17:39,867
knowing that this is
a high-profile case.

312
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,967
I'm sure Joey is also waiting
for an answer.

313
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:46,100
What did Major Delgado's body
look like

314
00:17:46,233 --> 00:17:48,067
after the explosion?

315
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:50,667
Was it really unrecognizable?

316
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:53,767
Actually, we didn't see it.

317
00:17:55,333 --> 00:17:58,733
They took the body very
carefully and privately

318
00:17:58,867 --> 00:18:01,300
out of respect
for Major Delgado.

319
00:18:02,767 --> 00:18:05,400
They also made sure
that the family didn't see it.

320
00:18:05,533 --> 00:18:07,633
because they might not be able
to handle it.

321
00:18:09,133 --> 00:18:12,067
So no one saw it
except the police?

322
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:17,333
This, this is okay.

323
00:18:18,033 --> 00:18:19,433
This is okay too.

324
00:18:19,833 --> 00:18:21,067
This too.

325
00:18:21,933 --> 00:18:23,567
But this, something is missing.

326
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:25,867
Better yet, complete it first

327
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,767
and then return it to me, okay?

328
00:18:30,533 --> 00:18:32,267
Okay, Sir,
I'll just fix it again.

329
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:36,133
Sir, how long will
the autopsy take?

330
00:18:36,267 --> 00:18:37,400
What else do they need to do?

331
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:39,567
Why can't we get Dad's remains?

332
00:18:40,567 --> 00:18:42,733
Joey, you have to understand

333
00:18:42,867 --> 00:18:45,033
that there was foul play
in what happened to Miguel.

334
00:18:45,167 --> 00:18:47,767
There's a lot that needs
to be investigated,

335
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:50,733
and it needs to be done
carefully and slowly,

336
00:18:50,867 --> 00:18:54,467
especially since the state of
your Dad's remains is dangerous.

337
00:18:55,367 --> 00:18:56,633
Well, Sir, but...

338
00:18:56,767 --> 00:18:58,200
- Perez.
- Sir?

339
00:18:58,333 --> 00:19:00,433
Where's the report
I'm asking you to take care of?

340
00:19:00,567 --> 00:19:02,067
Oh, here it is, Sir.

341
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,033
- Here, Sir.
- This is important.

342
00:19:06,933 --> 00:19:08,233
This is missing a signatory.

343
00:19:08,367 --> 00:19:09,500
Yes, Sir, I'll just
follow up again.

344
00:19:09,633 --> 00:19:10,767
- Okay, Sir.
- Thank you.

345
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:15,133
But, Sir, the autopsies probably
know what they're doing,

346
00:19:15,267 --> 00:19:18,000
so they know how long
the tests will take.

347
00:19:18,133 --> 00:19:20,267
Why can't they give us a
definite time

348
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:22,467
when we can see Dad?

349
00:19:23,933 --> 00:19:25,233
Joey...

350
00:19:25,367 --> 00:19:27,567
I can't really say right now.

351
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,833
Don't be in a hurry, okay?

352
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,500
This is for your dad.

353
00:19:33,033 --> 00:19:34,433
Go home,

354
00:19:34,567 --> 00:19:36,333
watch over Clarissa,

355
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:38,333
and we'll take care of this.

356
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:43,233
Ah, I'm sorry.

357
00:19:43,367 --> 00:19:45,100
I have to go somewhere else.

358
00:19:46,067 --> 00:19:47,367
- Oh, Perez.
- Sir?

359
00:19:47,500 --> 00:19:49,733
Leo's case.

360
00:19:49,867 --> 00:19:50,733
- Yes, Sir.
- Investigate it, okay?

361
00:19:50,867 --> 00:19:53,167
Yes, I'll follow it up
right away.

362
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,000
Hello, Sir Emerson,
I'm on my way there.

363
00:21:17,133 --> 00:21:18,233
Peter.

364
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:20,100
Sir?

365
00:21:20,233 --> 00:21:21,900
It's me, Jin Ho.

366
00:21:22,033 --> 00:21:23,167
Jin Ho?

367
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:25,767
Jin Ho<i> , what happened to you?
</i> Where are you?

368
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:26,933
<i>That's why I can't contact you,</i>

369
00:21:27,067 --> 00:21:29,100
you changed your number!

370
00:21:29,233 --> 00:21:30,567
Peter, listen.

371
00:21:30,933 --> 00:21:33,133
I only called to tell you...

372
00:21:33,267 --> 00:21:35,533
do not contact me again.

373
00:21:35,667 --> 00:21:37,933
Huh? What are you saying?

374
00:21:39,100 --> 00:21:40,767
Jin Ho, you need to know
something.

375
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:42,967
This is last time we talk.

376
00:21:43,133 --> 00:21:45,167
Something happened
to Joey's father.

377
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:46,600
<i> He's gone!</i>

378
00:21:46,733 --> 00:21:47,767
What?

379
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:50,567
Joey's father is dead, Jin Ho.

380
00:22:09,100 --> 00:22:10,600
Nothing?

381
00:22:19,067 --> 00:22:20,500
Joey!

382
00:22:26,833 --> 00:22:28,800
What are you doing here?

383
00:22:29,233 --> 00:22:30,667
Chief, where's Dad?

384
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:33,033
Why is his body not here?

385
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:48,500
I just have a strong hunch.

386
00:22:48,667 --> 00:22:50,433
I believe dad is still alive.

387
00:22:50,567 --> 00:22:51,500
If your dad is alive,

388
00:22:51,633 --> 00:22:53,100
why hasn't he come home
to you yet, right?

389
00:22:53,233 --> 00:22:55,267
If I only knew where he went.

390
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:57,167
You guys have finalized
the deal, huh?

391
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:58,767
Once we meet,
the deal is sealed.

392
00:22:58,900 --> 00:23:00,433
Just tell me about
Joey's father.

393
00:23:00,567 --> 00:23:01,867
He needs us now, Jin Ho.

394
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,033
I can't, I haven't found
her yet.

395
00:23:04,167 --> 00:23:06,933
Any news on Major Delgado's
DNA or autopsy?

396
00:23:07,067 --> 00:23:08,233
You know the protocol.

397
00:23:08,367 --> 00:23:10,500
Sir, how long are we going
to keep this?

398
00:23:10,633 --> 00:23:13,833
If anyone knows where he went,

399
00:23:13,967 --> 00:23:15,567
it's Lansang.

400
00:23:15,700 --> 00:23:19,800
Drug syndicate?
